tal, and modified Maritime air, affect the area under discussion in Winter. Weakening of the Asiatic High permits entrance or maritime air from Northwestern Europe and the Mediterranean, which brings most or the area's precipitation. Southwest winds in the wake or the cyclones traveling over the Mediterranean bring hot, dry, dusty winds from the southern deserts and are known in the various countries by different names.

